# Secrets and credentials
#
# e2e/tesbo.config.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is what `npx @tesbox/playwright-reporter
# init` writes, and it carries baseUrl, projectId and a project API token. The first two are not
# secrets and the SDK's README says to commit them; the token is, and it is committed here as an
# accepted, deliberate decision (2026-08-28) so that every CI runner has all three values with no
# credential plumbing — the alternative, two-of-three, is the SDK's `incomplete` state and fails the
# run at collection time.
#
# What that costs, so a future reader can weigh it rather than rediscover it: the token has `write`
# scope on project 41dba2a2-a60b-4917-8d63-9f8a86986703 only, it cannot read another project, and
# rotating it (Project -> Settings -> API & MCP) does not remove it from this repo's history. If the
# repo is ever opened up, rotate first. Precedence is inline options, then env, then this file, so
# a runner that sets TESBO_API_TOKEN still overrides the committed value without editing anything.
infra/kubernetes/**/secret.yaml
infra/kubernetes/base/registry-secret.yaml
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks

